{
  "_": [
    "The film, as data. Nothing here is a time in seconds: every shot is placed",
    "and measured in BEATS, and film/build.py turns beats into frames with",
    "",
    "    frames_per_beat = fps * 60 / tempo_bpm = 24 * 60 / 144 = 10",
    "",
    "which is an integer, which is the whole reason for those two numbers. A cut",
    "therefore lands on an exact frame that is also an exact beat of the score,",
    "and film/score/compose.py derives its sections from THIS file, so the score",
    "grows with the film rather than the film being stretched to fit the score.",
    "",
    "320 beats = 80 bars = 133.333 s.",
    "",
    "Everything on screen is the window manager or an application. Source clips",
    "are listed in film/SOURCES.md with the result of the identity scan that",
    "cleared each one; the window manager and the chapter-four document are",
    "re-recorded by film/build.sh on every build."
  ],
